 "conclusions": [
  "No two origin markets rank destinations the same way. Germany goes to Austria, Switzerland, Sweden and Cyprus. Brazil goes to Portugal and almost nowhere else. Japan goes to Thailand and Malaysia. Spain goes to Switzerland, Thailand, Ireland and Andorra. The United States goes to Canada and Japan. A single global destination list would be wrong for ten of the eleven markets.",
  "Poland expresses relocation as work. Work in Germany is 7,100 a month and emigration to Germany is 30. The ratio is two hundred and thirty to one, and it means the Move families are the wrong entry point for pl-PL while the Work families are the right one.",
  "Cost per click and volume rank origins differently too. France has the smallest volumes and Britain the highest values: moving to France asked in Britain carries ninety cents a click and moving to Dubai a dollar, against two cents for the equivalent French phrasings.",
  "Taiwan is confirmed for the third time, by a third method, as an inbound rather than outbound market. It has Areas and Stay demand for Taipei and no measurable outbound relocation demand at all."
